# Customer Sales & Analytics (Excel)

## Overview
An Excel dashboard analyzing 3,900 retail purchases to understand sales by category, season, subscription status, shipping type and discounts.

## Dataset
- 3,900 purchases (one row per customer ID), 18 attributes
- Fields: Customer ID, Age, Gender, Item Purchased, Category, Purchase Amount (USD), Location, Size, Color, Season, Review Rating, Subscription Status, Shipping Type, Discount Applied, Promo Code Used, Previous Purchases, Payment Method, Frequency of Purchases

## What is in the workbook
- Sheets: Dashboard, vlookup, Pivot tables, data
- 6 PivotTables, 10 charts and 2 slicers
- INDEX-MATCH, VLOOKUP and SUMIF formulas

## Key metrics
- Total sales: $233,081
- Total purchases: 3,900
- Average review rating: 3.75
- Sales from discounted purchases: $99,411 (1,677 purchases, 43%)

## Findings
- Clothing is the top category at $104,264 (44.7% of sales), followed by Accessories ($74,200), Footwear ($36,093) and Outerwear ($18,524)
- Sales are spread evenly across seasons (about 24-26% each)
- Non-subscribers generate 73.1% of sales ($170,436)
- Discounted and non-discounted purchases have similar average amounts ($59.28 vs $60.13)

## Limits
- No date field, so time trends cannot be analyzed
- Discount is a Yes/No flag with no discount amount

## Files
- Ecommerce data analysis.xlsx: data, pivot tables and dashboard
- Ecom data analysis dashboard.png: dashboard preview
- Customer-Sales-and-Analytics-Report-final.pdf: report (see note below)

